        "category": "summary",
        "text": "Security update for buildah",
        "title": "Title of the patch"
      },
      {
        "category": "description",
        "text": "This update for buildah fixes the following issues\n\n- CVE-2026-39821: golang.org/x/net/idna: failure to reject ASCII-only Punycode-encoded labels allows for validation\n  bypass and privilege escalation (bsc#1266648).\n- CVE-2026-39829: golang.org/x/crypto/ssh: pathological RSA/DSA parameters may cause DoS (bsc#1266191).\n- CVE-2026-39830: golang.org/x/crypto/ssh: client can cause server deadlock on unexpected responses (bsc#1266191).\n- CVE-2026-46598: golang.org/x/crypto/ssh: pathological inputs can lead to client panic/agent (bsc#1266191).\n",
        "title": "Description of the patch"
      },
